BUILD A COMPLETE FULL-STACK AI DOCUMENT INTELLIGENCE PLATFORM CALLED DOCULENS

ROLE
Act as a senior product architect, full-stack engineer, AI engineer, document-processing engineer, security and privacy engineer, UI/UX designer, motion designer, and QA engineer, working together. Design, implement, run, and test a real, usable application — not a static prototype, not a landing-page-only site, not screens with no logic behind them. Never fake a working feature. If something needs credentials or infrastructure not yet configured, implement its real architecture, show a clear configuration state, and keep everything else functional.

PRODUCT
DOCULENS turns complicated documents into understandable insights, requirements, comparisons, warnings, and action plans.
Core promise: UPLOAD ANY DOCUMENT → UNDERSTAND IT → EXTRACT WHAT MATTERS → IDENTIFY WHAT IS REQUIRED → FIND WHAT IS MISSING → KNOW WHAT TO DO NEXT.
It must be fully useful with no AI key connected and no account created.
"DOCULENS" is a working name — store it in one config value so it can be renamed later without touching the codebase.

TARGET USERS — THIS IS NOT A STUDENT APP
Build for anyone who struggles to read, verify, or act on a document: students, parents, job seekers, employees, professionals, freelancers, individual applicants, small businesses, startups, large companies, NGOs, colleges and institutions, consultants and agencies, and general citizens dealing with official paperwork. Use one flexible profile model — do not build separate apps or separate flows per user type.

EXAMPLE USE CASES
- Student uploads a scholarship notice → amount, last date, eligibility, required documents, steps.
- Company uploads a government tender → eligibility, GST, turnover, experience, certificates, EMD, deadlines.
- Job seeker uploads a job description → required skills compared against their saved CV.
- Freelancer uploads a client contract → payment terms, deliverables, deadlines, penalties, termination, risks.
- College administrator uploads a circular → structured explanation and action checklist.
- A spreadsheet of applicants → counts, totals, duplicates, missing values, charts from real data.

